1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,675
Every textbook says the same thing.

2
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:06,670
Humans settled down, learned to farm, then built cities.

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,738
Göbekli Tepe is 12,000 years old.

4
00:00:09,738 --> 00:00:13,159
6,000 years before farming even existed.

5
00:00:13,159 --> 00:00:16,988
Local shepherds in Turkey always said the hilltop was sacred.

6
00:00:16,988 --> 00:00:19,954
Archaeologists ignored them for decades.

7
00:00:19,954 --> 00:00:24,079
In 1994, a German archaeologist started digging.

8
00:00:24,079 --> 00:00:26,284
Massive carved pillars.

9
00:00:26,284 --> 00:00:28,431
Built by hunter-gatherers.

10
00:00:28,431 --> 00:00:31,068
20 times older than the pyramids.

11
00:00:31,068 --> 00:00:34,738
And then, someone buried Göbekli Tepe on purpose.

12
00:00:34,738 --> 00:00:38,068
They didn't build temples because they had civilization.

13
00:00:38,068 --> 00:00:41,306
They built civilization because they had temples.

